# Independent executable Keccak / SHA3 review

The final repaired component passes **60 tests**: 25 independent controls in
`test_independent_keccak.py` and 35 owner controls. The final JUnit, log and
receipt record the exact command and ten selected source hashes before/after;
all were stable. This remains an ignored source-level component diagnostic.
No tracked source, Cargo job or native worker was changed or executed.
Production and all full qualification flags remain false.

One concrete API validation defect was found after the first 50 tests passed.
With default `lru_cache` key typing, after
`sha3_512_block(message_bytes=0)`, keyword calls with `False` and `0.0` returned
the cached block without reaching exact-integer validation. The cost function
had the same behavior. `cache-validation-counterexample.json` binds the
original helper identity and observed reproduction; `pre-cache-fix-*` keeps
the first 50-test result at that old candidate. The owner set `typed=True` on
both caches. Eight independent cases now warm 0/1 cache entries and refuse
their boolean/float equivalents for both block and cost functions. Two owner
cases cover the same defect. The repair does not change canonical integer
maps, gate counts, source byte semantics or the current validated kernel path.

The independent lane reference computes theta on whole 64-bit words and
performs rho/pi through an in-place 24-lane orbit, rather than the circuit's
bit scatter or the owner's inverse-coordinate word model. A continuous LFSR
derives all 24 round constants without restarting per-index. For rounds 0,
12 and 23 the actual clean emitted gates are interpreted simultaneously on
all 1,600 one-bit states and their complements, plus zero/all-ones. Every
input, arbitrary correlated target, external guard and workspace bit is
checked, and emitted X/CNOT/Toffoli counts are compared with the block count.
These finite samples are broad orientation and nonlinearity controls, not an
exhaustive 1,600-bit-domain proof.

A complete 24-round forward/copy circuit is checked against the independent
orbit model; deliberately omitting its inverse leaves correlated work despite
the correct permutation output. This distinguishes output equality from the
required clean joint-state map. The complete empty-message SHA3 clean circuit
is executed for both dummy-input values, with arbitrary targets and untouched
guards. The empty input bit is retained and does not affect the digest.

Padding controls remove the required suffix or final pad NOT at the 71-byte
and 72-byte boundaries, preserving all other nodes; every altered digest
differs from Python's independent SHA3-512 implementation. A separate mutant
omits the fresh final padding permutation after an exact rate block and also
fails. These controls exercise the distinction between SHA3 domain/padding,
full-block absorption and a generic unpadded Keccak computation. They do not
introduce another backend oracle.

Additional controls require malformed input/output/work wire labels to fail
before the first gate, authenticate the loaded IR path, and inject a change
only at the report's final source observation. The latter exits 1, publishes
the error diagnostic and keeps every qualification flag false. It does not
publish a successful construction after late drift.

The separate `construction-review.md` records the source/FIPS/count review.
The mathematical clean construction uses disjoint registers, fresh Boolean
history, output XOR and a reverse traversal. Its X/CNOT/Toffoli maps extend
linearly to coherent joint states under the clean-work interface. This does
not promise that an input's reduced state remains unchanged after it becomes
entangled with the output, and it does not support discarding dirty history.
Python/runtime integrity, compiler correspondence and complete dependency
closure remain outside these selected-source diagnostics.

No remaining blocking finding within the reviewed component scope. Static
message length, actual public framing/typing, coherent length selection,
whole-machine state/cleanup, physical resources, primitive advantages and
independent cryptographic acceptance remain separate obligations. The
concrete SHA3 implementation neither implements nor qualifies the simulator's
named immutable ideal base F.
